A single release binary built with `cargo`. The only dependency is
[`serde_json`](https://crates.io/crates/serde_json) for the MCP server — no MCP
SDK, no framework.

## Usage

```bash
{{name}} {{command}}          # the example command — replace with your own
{{name}} brief                # print an AI session-bootstrap context block
{{name}} version
{{name}} help
```

## The four surfaces

Scaffolded by [aiscaffold](https://github.com/danishvirani/aiscaffold). Everything is wired up:

- **CLI** — `src/main.rs`, a small Rust binary. Add commands by adding a match arm to `run`.
- **Claude Code plugin** — `plugins/{{name}}/`: a manifest, a slash command per CLI command, and an auto-loading bootstrap skill. Use it with `claude --plugin-dir ./plugins/{{name}}` or symlink it into `~/.claude/plugins/`.
- **MCP server** — `src/mcp.rs`, a hand-rolled stdio JSON-RPC server using only `serde_json`. Run it with `{{name}} mcp`.
- **brief command** — `{{name}} brief` prints a Markdown context block to paste at the start of an AI session, so the agent starts with the project's shape already loaded.

## Develop

```bash
./install.sh                 # cargo build --release → ~/.local/bin/{{name}}
cargo test
cargo clippy --all-targets
cargo fmt --check            # should print nothing
```

